.TH str_istr 3
.SH NAME
str_istr \- find a substring, case-insensitively
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "str.h"
.PP
.BI "char *str_istr(char *" s ", char *" find ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B str_istr
finds the first occurrence of string
.I find
within
.I s
using a case-insensitive comparison. It returns a pointer to the found
substring, or NULL if not found.
.SH SEE ALSO
str_case_diff(3)